<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  LOCAL OVERRIDE of robotiq_description's robotiq_2f_85_macro.urdf.xacro
  (vendored from /opt/ros/jazzy/share/robotiq_description/urdf/, package
  version installed 2026-08). Not edited in place there: that's a
  system-installed package, out of this repo's control and not something
  a workspace should patch underneath itself.

  CHANGES from upstream, all tagged "OVERRIDE 2026-08-10", six total:
  robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint and robotiq_85_right_knuckle_joint's
  <limit velocity="..."> dropped from 0.5 to 0.1. The other four linkage
  joints (left/right_inner_knuckle, left/right_finger_tip) had NO <limit>
  element at all upstream (confirmed by diff against the pristine
  package file, not assumed) and each gained one at velocity=0.1,
  effort=50, matching the master exactly. See the second WHY block below
  for why all six must be equal, not just the two that already had limits.

  WHY: gz_ros2_control's position command interface is not a position
  loop. GazeboSimSystem::write() converts a position command into a
  proportional VELOCITY command every control cycle
  (target_vel = -position_proportional_gain * error, gain=0.1 confirmed
  from this project's own sim logs, effective loop gain 0.1*500Hz=50/s)
  and writes that to Gazebo as JointVelocityCmd. Gazebo holds a
  velocity, never a position, for this joint. If the ros2_control loop
  stalls for any reason, the LAST WRITTEN VELOCITY persists and the joint
  keeps moving open-loop at whatever rate was last commanded, saturated
  at this <limit>, until the loop resumes. Overshoot = velocity times
  stall_duration. Two live m3_grasp trials showed the pre-close command
  (target 0.1055rad) travel to 0.52 to 0.56rad before correcting, a
  0.42 to 0.46rad excursion, consistent with a real but as-yet-unmeasured
  loop stall (see docs/m3_trace_goal_traffic.py,
  docs/m3_run_context_overshoot_test*.sh, scripts/stall_monitor.py).

  This override does not fix the stall itself; the cause is still being
  measured (scripts/stall_monitor.py, deployed passively going forward).
  It reduces the CONSEQUENCE by construction: overshoot is linear in
  velocity, so a 900ms stall now costs 0.09rad instead of 0.45rad,
  below grip_angle, harmless in free space, at the cost of the pre-close
  stroke taking about 5x longer (about 0.2s to about 1.0s for a 0.1rad
  travel), which nothing in this project's timeouts is tight against.
  Also directly serves the earlier-established ejection finding (closing
  rate is what turned a grasp into a 363mm ejection, 2.19x being the
  difference): the same lever, pointed at by two separate findings.

  SECOND WHY, for the four newly-limited followers: GazeboSimSystem's
  mimic-joint branch (bottom of write()) computes
  velocity_sp = -1.0 * position_error * update_rate against the follower's
  MEASURED position vs. the master's, with no gain factor: an effective
  500/s correction, ten times stiffer than the master's own 50/s P-loop,
  and previously no velocity ceiling of its own on four of the five
  followers. Measured consequence before this fix: with NO gripper goal
  active at all (mid Cartesian-descent, ~2s gap between the pre-close hold
  succeeding and the final-close goal being sent), the master was dragged
  0.0956 -> 0.2546rad while its own controller commanded full retreat
  toward 0.0956, and one sample read -0.3551rad/s, 3.5x the master's OWN
  velocity clamp at the time (0.1). A joint cannot exceed its own clamp
  under its own command; something else was moving it. The velocity value
  chosen (0.1) is not a margin, it is exactly the master's: every
  multiplier in this file is +-1.0, so a correctly-tracking follower needs
  no more than the master's rate, and equal limits mean a dragging
  follower can move at most as fast as the master's own retreat, letting
  the master's P-loop fight to a draw instead of losing outright. Any
  follower left with more headroom than the master keeps the drag's edge.
  Effort matched to the master's 50 for the same physical reason (same
  linkage); this is a second new constraint alongside velocity and is not
  assumed to contribute zero: if a later measurement shows less than
  proportional shrinkage in the drag, raising follower effort first is how
  the two constraints get separated, not by guessing.

  Trade of this fix: a follower that falls behind can never catch up while
  the master is moving (equal top speed, no headroom to close a gap).
  Watch for accumulating tracking error in six-joint traces going forward:
  something to measure, not to silently pre-compensate for.

  To pick up upstream changes: re-diff this file against the installed
  package (`diff /opt/ros/jazzy/share/robotiq_description/urdf/robotiq_2f_85_macro.urdf.xacro
  ur5e_robotiq_description/urdf/vendor/robotiq_2f_85_macro.urdf.xacro`)
  and reapply the six OVERRIDE edits on top of whatever changed upstream.

  SEVENTH OVERRIDE, 2026-08-11: effort 50 -> 13 on all six joints (the
  master's real limit; followers matched to it for the same "no more
  headroom than the master" reason as the six above, not re-derived).
  50 was never a physical value, inherited from wherever this vendor
  file's numbers originally came from, unexamined until instrumenting the
  effort state interface (added this session, see
  robotiq_gripper.ros2_control.xacro) made it measurable. DART enforces
  a joint's effort limit as a hard actuator torque cap, confirmed live: a
  measured hold-phase effort of 40 N*m, sitting right at the old 50 N*m
  ceiling, not a lower value the mechanism settled on by itself. At the
  ~55mm knuckle-to-pad-contact moment arm (from the same mesh geometry
  that gave pad_centre_offset; +-20% uncertain, not +-3x), 40 N*m is
  roughly 730 N of pad force, and a real 2F-85's rated max is 235 N
  (`gripper_max_force:=235.0` in the upstream macro's own params). The
  grip closing 5.4mm of aperture further during a single lift, against a
  rigid 45mm cube that cannot compress, is that force: the object left,
  it was not slipping.
  235 N * 0.055m = ~13 N*m is the derived replacement, not tuned to a
  result: holding a 0.15kg object at mu=1.0 needs 0.74 N of friction,
  so there is roughly an order of magnitude of headroom below 13 even
  before the moment-arm uncertainty above. If the object still leaves at
  13, the ceiling is still too high, not wrong in kind.

  EIGHTH OVERRIDE, 2026-08-11, same day: effort 13 -> 1.0. 13 N*m was
  still wrong, confirmed live: a 20-cycle sweep at that ceiling scored
  0/20, worse than the unphysical 50 N*m ceiling's 14/20, and the
  post-lift joint reading clustered tightly (0.4443-0.4602 rad across 18
  cycles) rather than scattering, a near-deterministic mechanism, not
  noise. A rigid cube between two closing pads is an unstable
  equilibrium; the 2F-85's own geometry biases the extrusion path, and
  the effort trace showed why: pinned at the ceiling for ~1.5s while
  position crept, then collapsed to ~0 as the object came free. Squeezing
  harder against an unstable equilibrium pushes it out faster, which is
  why 13 N*m did worse than 50, not better.
  1.0 N*m is not another interpolation toward a still-unphysical number,
  the actual required force is far below even 13's own derivation: pad
  mu=100000 (see the friction pass-through fix elsewhere in this file)
  means the real job is "maintain contact at all," not "grip hard," and
  holding 0.15kg at mu=1.0 needs 0.74 N of friction, so a generous 10 N of
  pad force is already 0.55 N*m through the ~55mm arm. 1.0 N*m is a large
  step down (13x) rather than another incremental sweep, deliberately: at
  13x a generous requirement there is enough room for a clear read
  (effort coming off the ceiling = stable equilibrium found) instead of
  another marginal, ambiguous result costing another 40-minute sweep.
  If effort is STILL pinned at 1.0 and the object still leaves, that is a
  structural finding, not a tuning one: position control on this joint
  always rails the velocity command once commanded past touch (see
  gripper_close_and_hold's hold-at-target fix), so effort will pin at
  whatever the ceiling is regardless of its value, and the fix at that
  point is an effort COMMAND interface, not a lower number.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://wiki.ros.org/xacro" name="robotiq_gripper">
    <xacro:macro name="robotiq_gripper" params="
        name
        prefix
        parent
        *origin
        sim_ignition:=false
        sim_isaac:=false
        use_fake_hardware:=false
        fake_sensor_commands:=false
        include_ros2_control:=true
        com_port:=/dev/ttyUSB0">

        <!-- ros2 control include -->
        <xacro:include filename="$(find ur5e_robotiq_description)/urdf/vendor/robotiq_gripper.ros2_control.xacro" />
        <!-- if we are simulating or directly communicating with the gripper we need a ros2 control instance -->
        <xacro:if value="${include_ros2_control}">
            <xacro:robotiq_gripper_ros2_control
                name="${name}" prefix="${prefix}"
                sim_ignition="${sim_ignition}"
                sim_isaac="${sim_isaac}"
                use_fake_hardware="${use_fake_hardware}"
                fake_sensor_commands="${fake_sensor_commands}"
                com_port="${com_port}"/>
        </xacro:if>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/robotiq_base.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/robotiq_base.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0.0 2.274e-05 0.03232288" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="6.6320197e-01" />
                <inertia ixx="5.1617816e-04" iyy="5.8802208e-04" izz="3.9462776e-04" ixy="2.936e-8" ixz="0.0" iyz="-3.2296e-7" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/left_knuckle.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/left_knuckle.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0.01213197 0.0002 -0.00058647" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="1.384773208e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="3.5232e-7" iyy="2.31944e-6" izz="2.23136e-6" ixy="0.0" ixz="1.1744e-7" iyz="0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_knuckle_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/right_knuckle.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/right_knuckle.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="-0.01213197 0.0002 -0.00058647" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="1.384773208e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="3.5232e-7" iyy="2.31944e-6" izz="2.23136e-6" ixy="0.0" ixz="-1.1744e-7" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/left_finger.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/left_finger.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0.00346899 -0.00079447 0.01867121" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="4.260376752e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="1.385792000000000e-05" iyy="1.183208e-05" izz="5.19672e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="-2.17264e-06" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/right_finger.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/right_finger.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="-0.00346899 -5.53e-06 0.01867121" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="4.260376752000000e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="1.385792e-05" iyy="1.183208e-05" izz="5.19672e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="2.17264e-06" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_inner_knuckle_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/left_inner_knuckle.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/left_inner_knuckle.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0.01897699 0.00015001 0.02247101" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="2.969376448e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="9.57136e-06" iyy="8.69056e-06" izz="8.19144e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="-3.93424e-06" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_inner_knuckle_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/right_inner_knuckle.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/right_inner_knuckle.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="-0.01926824 5.001e-05 0.02222178" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="2.969376448e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="9.42456e-06" iyy="8.69056e-06" izz="8.33824e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="3.9636e-06" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_tip_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/left_finger_tip.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/left_finger_tip.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="-0.01456706 -0.0008 0.01649701" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="4.268588744e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="1.048152e-05" iyy="1.197888e-05" izz="4.22784e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="3.5232e-6" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <!-- Fingertip friction/contact params live here, not inline in <collision>
             above: a bare <surface> nested inside a URDF <collision> is not part of
             the URDF schema libsdformat's URDF->SDF converter recognizes, and gets
             silently dropped at spawn (confirmed via `gz sdf -p`: the inline form
             produced zero <surface> elements anywhere in the converted SDF). This
             <gazebo reference> extension form is the one the converter actually
             keeps. Tag names are also SDFormat 1.11's current names, not the old
             Gazebo-classic ones the inline block used (mu1 to mu, minDepth to
             min_depth, maxVel to max_vel), verified via `gz sdf -p` producing zero
             "not defined in SDF" warnings on this form, vs. one per old-style tag
             name otherwise. -->
        <gazebo reference="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_tip_link">
            <collision>
                <surface>
                    <friction>
                        <ode>
                            <mu>100000.0</mu>
                            <mu2>100000.0</mu2>
                        </ode>
                    </friction>
                    <contact>
                        <ode>
                            <kp>1e+5</kp>
                            <kd>1</kd>
                            <soft_cfm>0</soft_cfm>
                            <soft_erp>0.2</soft_erp>
                            <min_depth>0.002</min_depth>
                            <max_vel>0</max_vel>
                        </ode>
                    </contact>
                </surface>
            </collision>
        </gazebo>

        <link name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_tip_link">
            <visual>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/visual/right_finger_tip.dae" />
                </geometry>
            </visual>
            <collision>
                <geometry>
                    <mesh filename="file://$(find robotiq_description)/meshes/collision/right_finger_tip.stl" />
                </geometry>
            </collision>
            <inertial>
                <origin xyz="0.01456706 5e-05 0.01649701" rpy="0 0 0" />
                <mass value="4.268588744e-02" />
                <inertia ixx="1.048152e-05" iyy="1.197888e-05" izz="4.22784e-06" ixy="0.0" ixz="-3.5232e-06" iyz="0.0" />
            </inertial>
        </link>

        <gazebo reference="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_tip_link">
            <collision>
                <surface>
                    <friction>
                        <ode>
                            <mu>100000.0</mu>
                            <mu2>100000.0</mu2>
                        </ode>
                    </friction>
                    <contact>
                        <ode>
                            <kp>1e+5</kp>
                            <kd>1</kd>
                            <soft_cfm>0</soft_cfm>
                            <soft_erp>0.2</soft_erp>
                            <min_depth>0.002</min_depth>
                            <max_vel>0</max_vel>
                        </ode>
                    </contact>
                </surface>
            </collision>
        </gazebo>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${parent}" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link" />
            <xacro:insert_block name="origin" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" type="revolute">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="0.03060114 0.0 0.05490452" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: velocity 0.5 -> 0.1, see file header -->
            <limit lower="0.0" upper="0.8" velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_knuckle_joint" type="revolute">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_knuckle_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="-0.03060114 0.0 0.05490452" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: velocity 0.5 -> 0.1, see file header -->
            <limit lower="-0.8" upper="0.0" velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
            <mimic joint="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" multiplier="-1" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_link" />
            <origin xyz="0.03152616 0.0 -0.00376347" rpy="0 0 0" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_joint" type="fixed">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_knuckle_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_link" />
            <origin xyz="-0.03152616 0.0 -0.00376347" rpy="0 0 0" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_inner_knuckle_joint" type="continuous">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_inner_knuckle_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="0.0127 0.0 0.06142" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: added, was unlimited. See file header:
                 gz_ros2_control's mimic correction runs at 500/s with no
                 gain factor and no ceiling of its own; a follower with no
                 <limit> can drag the master through the linkage. Matches
                 the master's velocity (0.1) and effort (now 13, see
                 SEVENTH OVERRIDE below; matched at whatever the master's
                 own value is, not independently) exactly: every
                 multiplier here is +-1.0, so a correctly-tracking follower
                 needs no more than the master's own rate. -->
            <limit velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
            <mimic joint="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_inner_knuckle_joint" type="continuous">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_base_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_inner_knuckle_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="-0.0127 0.0 0.06142" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: added, was unlimited. See file header. -->
            <limit velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
            <mimic joint="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" multiplier="-1" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_tip_joint" type="continuous">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_finger_tip_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="0.00563134 0.0 0.04718515" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: added, was unlimited. See file header. -->
            <limit velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
            <mimic joint="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" multiplier="-1" />
        </joint>

        <joint name="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_tip_joint" type="continuous">
            <parent link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_link" />
            <child link="${prefix}robotiq_85_right_finger_tip_link" />
            <axis xyz="0 -1 0" />
            <origin xyz="-0.00563134 0.0 0.04718515" rpy="0 0 0" />
            <!-- OVERRIDE 2026-08-10: added, was unlimited. See file header. -->
            <limit velocity="0.1" effort="1.0" />
            <mimic joint="${prefix}robotiq_85_left_knuckle_joint" />
        </joint>
    </xacro:macro>
</robot>
